<% content_for :title, "GitReward — bounties that pay themselves" %>
<% repo_url = "https://github.com/gitreward/gitreward" %>

<%# ambient web3 backdrop: faint grid, fixed behind all content %>
<div class="lp-bg" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="lp-grid"></div>
</div>

<div class="wrap screen lp">
  <section class="lp-hero">
    <h1 class="lp-title">
      Bounties for GitHub issues<br>
      that <span class="lp-grad">pay themselves.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="lp-lede">
      Fund an issue in USDC. When the PR merges, the contributor gets paid
      automatically — no claim, no invoice, no middleman.
    </p>

    <div class="hero-cta">
      <%= button_to github_auth_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false }, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-glow" do %>
        <%= github_mark(17) %>
        Sign in with GitHub
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to "#how", class: "btn btn-ghost btn-lg" do %>
        How it works
        <%= icon(:arrow, 15) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%= link_to repo_url, class: "lp-os", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" do %>
      Open source &amp; self-hostable — run it fee-free
      <%= icon(:arrow, 13) %>
    <% end %>

    <div class="lp-trust">
      <div class="lp-trust-item">
        <%= icon(:lock, 16) %>
        <span>Non-custodial escrow</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-trust-item">
        <%= icon(:check, 16) %>
        <span>Auto-payout on merge</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-trust-item">
        <%= icon(:refund, 16) %>
        <span>Refunded if unsolved</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how" class="lp-steps-wrap" style="scroll-margin-top: 80px">
    <div class="lp-sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow accent">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="lp-sec-title">Three steps. The merge does the rest.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-steps">
      <div class="lp-step">
        <span class="lp-step-num">01</span>
        <div class="feature-icon"><%= icon(:pin, 22) %></div>
        <h3 class="h-sec">Post a bounty</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Pick one of your open issues and fund it with USDC. The funds lock in an open-source escrow contract on Base — you only pay gas.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-step">
        <span class="lp-step-num">02</span>
        <div class="feature-icon"><%= icon(:pull_request, 22) %></div>
        <h3 class="h-sec">Solve &amp; merge</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Contributors open a PR that closes the issue. Merge it into your target branch — the merge is the authorization, nothing else to click.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-step">
        <span class="lp-step-num">03</span>
        <div class="feature-icon"><%= icon(:circle_dollar, 22) %></div>
        <h3 class="h-sec">Get paid</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">The bounty disburses automatically to the contributor's linked wallet, minus a small fee. Unmatched bounties refund to the funder on a timer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="pricing" class="lp-pricing" style="scroll-margin-top: 80px">
    <div class="lp-sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow accent">Pricing</span>
      <h2 class="lp-sec-title">Fair fees, or none at all.</h2>
      <p class="sub">Use the hosted service for a flat cut on payout, or self-host the open-source stack and pay nothing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-price-grid">
      <div class="lp-price lp-price-feature">
        <div class="lp-price-head">
          <span class="lp-price-name">Hosted</span>
          <span class="badge badge-funded">Recommended</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-price-amt">
          <span class="lp-price-num">3%</span>
          <span class="lp-price-per">per paid bounty</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-desc">We run the neutral oracle and infrastructure. You just fund an issue and merge the PR.</p>
        <ul class="lp-price-list">
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> Charged only on a successful payout</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> Hard-capped at 10% in the contract — we can't charge more</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> Neutral hosted oracle signs every payout</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> No fee on refunds, ever</li>
        </ul>
        <%= button_to github_auth_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false }, class: "btn btn-primary btn-block btn-glow" do %>
          <%= github_mark(16) %>
          Sign in with GitHub
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-price">
        <div class="lp-price-head">
          <span class="lp-price-name">Self-hosted</span>
          <span class="badge badge-open">Open source</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-price-amt">
          <span class="lp-price-num">0%</span>
          <span class="lp-price-per">set your own fee</span>
        </div>
        <p class="card-desc">Run GitReward for your own organization. Call <code class="code-chip">setFeeRate(0)</code> and pay nothing.</p>
        <ul class="lp-price-list">
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> MIT-licensed escrow contracts on Base</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> AGPL-3.0 platform — deploy the whole stack</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> You run your own oracle and treasury</li>
          <li><%= icon(:check, 15) %> No protocol cut — keep 100%</li>
        </ul>
        <%= link_to repo_url, class: "btn btn-ghost btn-block", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" do %>
          <%= github_mark(16) %>
          View on GitHub
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="faq" style="scroll-margin-top: 80px">
    <div class="lp-sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow accent">Trust &amp; custody</span>
      <h2 class="lp-sec-title">How your money is handled</h2>
      <p class="sub">Plain English — non-custodial, one neutral oracle, you only pay gas to fund.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">Where does the money sit?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">In an open-source escrow contract on Base — not in our bank account. We can't spend it and we can't stop a refund. You only pay gas to fund it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">What do I actually trust you with?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">One thing: when a bounty PR is merged, we (a single neutral oracle) sign a message that says “pay this contributor.” The contract checks our signature and pays out. That signature is the only power we hold — and it can only pay the address the contributor themselves linked. It cannot redirect funds anywhere else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">What if GitReward disappears?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">Every unmatched bounty refunds to the funder after its expiry, with no action from us and no fee. The self-refund timer is the backstop — no one can strand your money, even if we vanish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">How does a contributor get paid?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">They link a payout wallet once, then solve issues normally. On merge, the bounty disburses to that wallet automatically — no claim step, no invoice. If they haven't linked a wallet by merge time, the bounty simply refunds to the maintainer at expiry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">What's the fee?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">3% on the hosted service, charged only when a bounty pays out — well under the 20%+ that's normal elsewhere. It's hard-capped <em>in the contract</em> at 10%, so we literally cannot charge more, by design. Self-hosters set the fee to zero and run fee-free.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">Is it really “trustless”?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">No — and we won't claim that. It's non-custodial with one neutral oracle. That's an honest, smaller claim than “trustless,” and it's the one we can actually stand behind.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-cta">
    <span class="eyebrow accent">Get started</span>
    <h2 class="lp-cta-title">Fund your first issue<br>in minutes.</h2>
    <p class="lp-cta-sub">Sign in with GitHub, pick an open issue, lock USDC. The merge pays it out.</p>
    <%= button_to github_auth_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false }, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-glow" do %>
      <%= github_mark(17) %>
      Sign in with GitHub
    <% end %>
  </section>
</div>
